## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Content Management with PayloadCMS (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Enable admins to create, read, update, and delete all content types through PayloadCMS admin interface with the same structure and relationships as Sanity CMS

**Independent Test**: Access PayloadCMS admin UI, create sample documents for each content type, verify all fields/validations/relationships function correctly

### Collection Schema Definitions

- [X] T013 [P] [US1] Create Video collection in payload/collections/Video.ts with all fields per data-model.md (title, slug, youtubeUrl, youtubeId, duration, category, ageRange, tags, notes, viewCount, lastViewedAt)
- [X] T014 [P] [US1] Create Category collection in payload/collections/Category.ts with hierarchical fields per data-model.md (name, slug, description, icon, ageRange, parent, fullPath, depth, isAgeRangeRoot, sortOrder, isVisible, childCount, videoCount, notes)
