## Dependencies & Execution Order

### Phase Dependencies

- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies - can start immediately
- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup completion - BLOCKS all user stories
- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Foundational (Phase 2) completion
- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on User Story 1 completion (needs collections defined before migration)
- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: Depends on User Story 2 completion (needs migrated data for frontend to consume)
- **User Story 4 (Phase 6)**: Depends on User Story 2 completion (scripts need PayloadCMS data to operate on)
- **User Story 5 (Phase 7)**: Depends on User Stories 3 AND 4 completion (frontend and scripts must work with PayloadCMS before removing Sanity)
- **Polish (Phase 8)**: Depends on all user stories completion

### User Story Dependencies

```text
Setup (Phase 1)
    ↓
Foundational (Phase 2) ← CRITICAL BLOCKER
    ↓
User Story 1 (Phase 3) ← MVP - PayloadCMS collections setup
    ↓
User Story 2 (Phase 4) ← Data migration
    ↓ ↘
User Story 3 (Phase 5)   User Story 4 (Phase 6)
(Frontend)               (Admin scripts)
    ↓                        ↓
    └─────→ User Story 5 (Phase 7) ← Sanity removal
               ↓
           Polish (Phase 8)
```

### Within Each User Story

**User Story 1 (PayloadCMS Setup)**:
- All collection schema files (T013-T018) can be created in parallel [P]
- Hooks and validations (T019-T032) must follow their respective collection creation
- Collection integration (T033-T035) after all collections and hooks complete
- Admin UI testing (T036-T042) at the end to validate everything works

**User Story 2 (Data Migration)**:
- All migration script files (T043-T046) can be created in parallel [P]
- Export → Transformation → Import → Verification (sequential execution: T047-T075)
- Error handling and validation within each script runs as part of that script's implementation

**User Story 3 (Frontend Integration)**:
- API client functions (T078-T085) after client creation (T076-T077)
- All component updates (T086-T093) can be done in parallel after API client ready
- Activity logging (T094-T098) can be done in parallel with component updates
- Environment config (T099-T100) can be done anytime
- Frontend testing (T101-T108) at the end to validate integration

**User Story 4 (Admin Scripts)**:
- Script identification (T109-T110) must complete first
- All script updates (T111-T115) can be done in parallel [P] after identification
- Script testing (T116-T120) for each script after its update completes

**User Story 5 (Sanity Removal)**:
- Pre-removal validation (T121-T124) must complete first (CRITICAL)
- All code removal tasks (T125-T132) can be done in parallel [P] after validation
- All documentation updates (T133-T137) can be done in parallel [P] with code removal
- Validation (T138-T144) at the end to confirm clean removal

### Parallel Opportunities

Within each phase:

**Phase 1 (Setup)**: T002-T005 can all run in parallel [P]

**Phase 2 (Foundational)**: T008-T012 can all run in parallel [P]

**Phase 3 (User Story 1)**:
- Collection schemas: T013-T018 in parallel
- After collections ready, can parallelize some hooks for different collections if they don't depend on each other

**Phase 4 (User Story 2)**:
- Script file creation: T043-T046 in parallel
- Execution is sequential (export → transform → import → verify)

**Phase 5 (User Story 3)**:
- API client function implementation: T078-T085 can be split among multiple devs
- Component updates: T086-T093 in parallel (different files)
- Activity logging: T094-T098 in parallel (different files)

**Phase 6 (User Story 4)**:
- Script updates: T111-T115 in parallel (different files)

**Phase 7 (User Story 5)**:
- Code removal: T125-T132 in parallel (different files)
- Documentation: T133-T137 in parallel (different files)

**Phase 8 (Polish)**:
- All documentation and review tasks: T145-T152 in parallel

---

## Parallel Example: User Story 1 Collection Creation

```bash
# Launch all collection schema files together:
Task T013: "Create Video collection in payload/collections/Video.ts"
Task T014: "Create Category collection in payload/collections/Category.ts"  
Task T015: "Create User collection in payload/collections/User.ts"
Task T016: "Create ActivityLog collection in payload/collections/ActivityLog.ts"
Task T017: "Create AdPlacement collection in payload/collections/AdPlacement.ts"
Task T018: "Create AffiliatePartner collection in payload/collections/AffiliatePartner.ts"

# Then once all schemas are created, launch their respective hooks:
Task T019: "Implement beforeValidate hook for Video in payload/hooks/videoHooks.ts"
Task T021: "Implement beforeValidate hook for Category in payload/hooks/categoryHooks.ts"
Task T024: "Implement beforeChange hook for User in payload/hooks/userHooks.ts"
# ... etc
```

